d standard military equipment. So a \u201cwell regulated\u201d army was simply one that was \u201cwell equipped\u201d and organized. \r\n\r\nIt does not refer to a professional army. The 17th century folks used the term \u201cstanding army\u201d or \u201cregulars\u201d to describe a professional army. \r\n\r\n**Therefore, \u201ca well regulated militia\u201d only means a well equipped militia that was organized and maintained internal discipline**. It does not imply, in any way,  the modern meaning of \u201cregulated,\u201d which means controlled or administered by some superior entity.", "author": "Bullet3250", "created": 1794749860019, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Bullet3250", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Sunday Gunday 2A key fact:  IMPORTANT NOTE: Back in the 18th century, a \u201cregular\u201d army meant  . . . ", "last_comment_created": 1794753694299, "content": "<p>IMPORTANT NOTE: Back in the 18th century, a \u201cregular\u201d army meant an army that had standard military equipment. So a \u201cwell regulated\u201d army was simply one that was \u201cwell equipped\u201d and organized.</p>\n<p>It does not refer to a professional army. The 17th century folks used the term \u201cstanding army\u201d or \u201cregulars\u201d to describe a professional army.</p>\n<p><strong>Therefore, \u201ca well regulated militia\u201d only means a well equipped militia that was organized and maintained internal discipline</strong>. It does not imply, in any way,  the modern meaning of \u201cregulated,\u201d which means controlled or administered by some superior entity.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 37, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToiHUrBI", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 54, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8940810, "raw_content": "", "author": "raptoris", "created": 1794741510814, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "-f-b-i-", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "news.northropgrumman.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://news.northropgrumman.com/b-21/b-21-raider-advances-into-weapons-testing", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "B-21 Raider Advances into Weapons Testing", "last_comment_created": 1794752661202, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 9, "score_up": 54, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Edwards AFB, Calif. \u2013 Nov. 13, 2026 \u2013 Northrop Grumman\u2019s B-21 Raider aircraft has demonstrated weapons release capability, marking a major step forward for America\u2019s next-generation bomber.", "title": "B-21 Raider Advances into Weapons Testing"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2121657428773052791", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToiHSvuG", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 763, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8940124, "raw_content": "", "author": "Diana", "created": 1794689262737, "profile_pi